  "limits": [
    "Test pause is after capture and before replay. Mutex access is observed during that pause; outside-lock replay placement is source-reviewed and replay-call count is instrumented. No full-duration mutex latency, hard CPU/RSS or cancellation deadline claim.",
    "Normal native activation remains false. No public-network request, native candidate, UI/CUA campaign or platform-specific Windows execution in this slice.",
    "Private capture/refusal bounds remain operational limits, not a new canonical quota state. No persisted cache or record/schema/policy migration.",
    "Initial attach/start, public inspect/page/cancel/resume, startup recovery and direct store Advance retain existing potentially mutex-held replay. Capture metadata, final source hashing and canonical I/O remain mutex-held.",
    "A fresh backwards/future Cancel or Advance is still refused without a charge. Existing receipt settlement preserves its narrower anchored stop, raw clock and canonical Cancel replay semantics.",
    "Original/acquisition source-media reinterpretation limitations and every release gate are unchanged."
